        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=2,\\ B=1,\\ C=-1$.",
          "worked": "Expand and collect like terms.\n$$Ax^2+(A+B)x+B+C=2x^2+3x.$$\nEquate the coefficients of $x^2$ and $x$, then the constant terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=2\\\\A+B&=3\\\\2+B&=3\\\\B&=1\\\\B+C&=0\\\\1+C&=0\\\\C&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p60-task-21-22-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p60-q22-identity",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "A(x-1)^2+B(x-1)+C=2x^2-x+4",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=2,\\ B=3,\\ C=5$.",
          "worked": "Expand and collect like terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}Ax^2-2Ax+A+Bx-B+C&=2x^2-x+4\\\\Ax^2+(B-2A)x+A-B+C&=2x^2-x+4\\end{align*}$$\nEquate the coefficients of $x^2$ and $x$, then the constant terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=2\\\\B-2A&=-1\\\\B-2(2)&=-1\\\\B&=3\\\\A-B+C&=4\\\\2-3+C&=4\\\\C&=5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
